  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** The company’s existing Platinum instrument business remains nascent, generating minimal commercial revenue with a modestly widening consumables mix. The investment narrative centers entirely on the Proteus next-generation protein sequencing platform, which has just achieved a key technical milestone by detecting 17 amino acids on fully integrated instruments. Management projects detection of all 20 amino acids during 2026 and a full sequencing kit in 2027, keeping the firm in a pre-revenue R&D posture for its target proteomics market. No immediate macro, regulatory, or competitive threats appear in the recent commentary.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership is combining heavy R&D investment with disciplined SG&A management, delivering a narrower-than-expected loss and emphasizing expense control. The team is providing a concrete, milestone-based Proteus roadmap (17 amino acids now, 18 by year-end, all 20 during 2026, kit in 2027) to build confidence in the platform’s progress. However, the tiny commercial base and a slight revenue miss highlight early-stage execution risk. The narrative relies heavily on forward-looking technical achievements, with little independent analyst scrutiny evident in the largely automated earnings summaries. Credibility hinges on meeting the near-term amino-acid detection targets.",
